    <Folder>
      <name>Candidate fields (not exact formation sites)</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>2002-06 - Barton Hills</name>
        <styleUrl>#candidate</styleUrl>
        <description>&lt;b&gt;Barton Hills&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Hertfordshire, England&lt;br&gt;Date: 2002-06 (qualified)&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Location role: candidate_field&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Coordinate method: legacy_coordinate_historical_image_scale_north_up; uncertainty 0.03 km&lt;br&gt;Explicit outcome: coordinate_size_geometry_provisional. The legacy point and matching north-up historical frame identify the Barton Hills near Hexton field, while the case-specific source labels the event 2002-07-22 and the canonical PDF records only early June; that date conflict is preserved. The measured 30 metre scale bar constrains the display footprint, but there are zero independent geographic checkpoints. The candidate and reviewed footprint remain excluded from formal alignment calculations and the source pixels are link-only.&lt;br&gt;Sources: Crop Circle Center PDF catalog&lt;br&gt;https://www.cropcirclecenter.com/</description>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="formation_id">
            <value>cc_96878ba19702</value>
