            <value>possible_candidate</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="orientation_status">
            <value>diagram_only_no_true_north</value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>-0.3915778131514003,51.94603793928447,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>2002-06-21 - Waden Hill</name>
        <styleUrl>#candidate</styleUrl>
        <description>&lt;b&gt;Waden Hill&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Wiltshire, England&lt;br&gt;Date: 2002-06-21 (day)&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Location role: candidate_field&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Coordinate method: legacy_coordinate_historical_image_scale_north_up; uncertainty 0.04 km&lt;br&gt;Explicit outcome: coordinate_size_geometry_provisional. The legacy jingjang description, the 2002 Waden Hill catalog diagram, and CRA event code ENWI200206 crosswalk to the same formation. The legacy coordinate plus the historical frame 30 metre scale bar and publisher-stated north-up constrain a display footprint, but zero independent checkpoints validate its corners. It remains excluded from formal alignment calculations and the source pixels are link-only.&lt;br&gt;Sources: Crop Circle Center PDF catalog&lt;br&gt;https://www.cropcirclecenter.com/</description>
