        <Point>
          <coordinates>-1.855548044334824,51.42454302630362,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>2002-06-27 - Dodworth</name>
        <styleUrl>#candidate</styleUrl>
        <description>&lt;b&gt;Dodworth&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;South Yorkshire, England&lt;br&gt;Date: 2002-06-27 (day)&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Location role: candidate_field&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Coordinate method: legacy_coordinate_historical_image_scale_north_up; uncertainty 0.04 km&lt;br&gt;Explicit outcome: coordinate_size_geometry_provisional. The legacy Dodworth point, distinctive pentagram catalog diagram, corn550 ground photograph, and ENYS200201 historical north-up frame identify the same St John the Baptist Church near Dodworth event. The canonical catalog date is June 27 while the Galactic listing says June 29; that conflict is preserved. The measured 30 metre scale bar constrains a display footprint, but zero independent checkpoints validate the corners. The 40 metre candidate remains excluded from formal alignment calculations and source pixels are link-only.&lt;br&gt;Sources: Crop Circle Center PDF catalog&lt;br&gt;https://www.cropcirclecenter.com/</description>
